well while we've seen a fair amount of  inter-korean projects between north and  south korea  going forward there's been far less  progress  between the united states and pyongyang  several high-level talks been cancelled  and have yet to be  rescheduled in his speech kim as you  mentioned  says that he wants to meet with donald  trump again in the new year  and trump has said that he is also  interested in that  and so what this uh what many will be  looking for out of that summit will be  specific some kind of agreement that  both sides can uh  work towards in the future that they  didn't get in their last summit  yeah so each side does appear to be  convinced that the other has done little  to fulfill  previous promises so what do they each  need to see  in order to be convinced  well at the very basic level they need  to have an agreement what they came out  of  from the singapore summit was basically  a series of very broad goals  and that has left a lot to be argued  over since then  and so i think many analysts will be  looking for again specifics out of  uh uh any future meeting an actual  agreement some kind of even limited road  map  um that both sides could potentially  agree on uh  and then compare uh you know progress  good talking to you thanks for joining  us uh josh smith in seoul  thank you
 

